� Q14: What is the importance of the HttpOnly flag on cookies? 
Candidate Answer: 
"The HttpOnly flag prevents JavaScript from accessing cookies. This is critical because in case 
of a Cross-site Scripting (XSS) attack, an attacker won't be able to steal session cookies via 
document.cookie. 
It’s especially important for session management cookies, because preventing access via 
JavaScript helps reduce the risk of session hijacking. 
However, it does not stop the cookie from being sent with every HTTP request — it only 
protects it from being accessed through client-side scripts." 
