� Q21: Can you explain SQL Injection and its types? 
Candidate Answer: 
"SQL Injection occurs when unsanitized input is used to dynamically construct SQL queries. 
Types include: 
• Classic SQLi: ' OR 1=1 -- 
• Error-based SQLi: Triggering SQL errors to leak data 
• Blind SQLi: No errors or output, using Boolean or Time-based inference 
• Union-based SQLi: Using UNION SELECT to extract data 
• Second-order SQLi: Payload stored and later executed in different context 
I test using payloads like ' OR '1'='1 or time delays like SLEEP(5) in suspected inputs." 
