� Q28: What is SSL Pinning and how do you bypass it? 
Candidate Answer: 
"SSL Pinning is a technique used in mobile apps to prevent MITM attacks. The app has a copy 
of the server's certificate (or public key) and validates the certificate chain manually, rather than 
relying on the system trust store. 
To bypass SSL pinning: 
• I first try runtime hooking using Frida with SSL pinning bypass scripts. 
• If that fails, I recompile the APK using JADX + apktool, remove the pinning 
logic (e.g., TrustManager, HostnameVerifier), and rebuild the app. 
• Tools like Objection or Xposed modules like JustTrustMe also help in dynamic 
bypass." 
