� Q59: What is the difference between path traversal and directory listing? 
Candidate Answer: 
"Directory listing allows browsing contents of a directory if index files are missing and listing is 
enabled — e.g., listing all /uploads/. 
Path traversal is a vulnerability where attackers navigate to parent directories using ../, to 
access files outside the allowed scope. 
Directory listing is a misconfiguration; path traversal is an actual vulnerability that can lead to 
credential or source code exposure." 
